{{- /*
prompt_wrapup is the one message a cut-off intent stage's agent is sent, in its own session, when its first run
stopped at its turn limit: write (a plan) or confirm against the working tree (a build) the report, with the few turns
held back for it. It is patchy's fixed text, paths and numbers alone: nothing untrusted is quoted.
*/ -}}
## You reached your turn limit

Your run stopped at its limit of {{.FirstTurns}} agent turns before it finished.
patchy gives you at most {{.Turns}} more turns to wrap up, and nothing more after them.
{{- if .CommitScriptPath}}

The working tree is kept exactly as it is now: patchy refuses a wrap-up that changes any file in it, and commits only
what it already holds.

- Do not edit code or tests, do not run tests, builds or other commands, and do not commit.
{{- if .ReportWritten}}
- Check the report you wrote at {{code .ReportPath}} against the working tree, and rewrite it
  so it describes what the tree holds now, in the format your instructions gave.
{{- else}}
- Write your report at {{code .ReportPath}} so it describes what the working tree holds now, in the format your
  instructions gave.
{{- end}}
- If the plan is not fully built, or its tests did not run and pass on the tree as it stands, set `success: false` and
  say in `reason` what is unfinished. Never claim more than the tree holds.
- Only if `success` is true: make sure {{code .CommitScriptPath}} exists and commits the change exactly as the tree
  holds it, and nothing else.
{{- else}}

- Stop exploring: read nothing more unless one read is needed to finish.
- Write your report at {{code .ReportPath}} now, in the format your instructions gave, from what you have
  already read. Say plainly in it what you did not get to check, and set your confidence to match, rather than
  guessing.
- Write no file but the report.
{{- end}}
- When you are done, reply with one short line saying so.
